            }
          ],
          "status": "documented",
          "value": "format names the layout type to use. allowedTypes lists permitted content types, restrictedTypes lists excluded content types, and restrictedTypes takes priority over allowedTypes. Layout nodes, counted from the outermost node through rows, columns and elements, can be nested at most four levels deep. The whole item is checked on every save, so content nested past a limit cannot be saved, even after an unrelated edit, until its nesting is reduced; a REST request that exceeds a limit returns 400 Bad Request with the path of the field."
        },
        "nativeType": {
          "evidence": [
